==============================================================================
(H) UNIFORM-IN-VMAX PROBE (the crux of GAP A): drive 2 coordinated parked
    speeds large on easy 11-core base11={1,2,3,5,7,8,9,10,11,12,13}.
==============================================================================
  As vmax -> infinity, L does NOT decay to 0; it PLATEAUS ~0.0238 (scale-1 L=0.01295).
  Random large coordinated parked pairs: min L = 0.01573 > 0.
  => Empirically, finer/larger coordinated combs tile more uniformly but their TOTAL
     mass-kill SATURATES; they cannot consume the base core's lonely set. This is the
     structural fact GAP A needs (meas bounded below uniformly in vmax) -- supported
     numerically, NOT proved. OPEN-Q-108 remains open.
